  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 206 AM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nCooler but benign weather is expected for the Thanksgiving holiday \nweek once the cold front and associated mid-level shortwave trough \nthat is moving through the area exits this morning. The cold front \nin question is bisecting the forecast area early this morning and \nshould make its way through the remainder of the forecast area by \nsunrise. Showers with this front will continue through sunrise but \nmay linger through mid-morning until the mid-level shortwave exits \nthe region. Behind the front, modest CAA is ongoing and is expected \nto continue through the day today. This will return highs to near \nnormal in the mid 40s to lower 50s. CAA will diminish tonight as a \nsurface ridge of high pressure begins to build into the area from \nthe northern Plains. Mostly clear skies and light northerly winds \nwill allow low to drop below freezing into the mid to upper 20s. \nThis surface ridge will then look to be the main feature of interest \nfor the local area Monday through Wednesday. Weak mixing Monday will \nhold temperatures in the 40s. Tuesday, will be the coolest day of \nthe forecast period as weak mixing continues under mostly cloudy \nskies coming courtesy of upper level trough moving through the \nregion. This will hold highs 5 to 10 degrees below normal in the \nupper 30s to mid 40s. weak mixing continues on Wednesday but again \nunder partly cloudy skies allow high to rise back into the low to \nmid 40s. Wednesday night a weak back door cold front will move \nthrough the area but the modest northerly fetch behind the front on \nThanksgiving will actually provide deeper mixing allowing highs to \nrise a couple degrees while remaining in the 40s. Friday, northerly \nflow aloft relaxes and becomes more zonal while late day WAA should \naid in highs rising into the mid 40s to lower 50s. Friday into \nFriday night a upper level trough will dig from the northern Plains \ninto the Midwest. This will force a dry cold front through the area. \nDecent westerly/west-northwesterly winds behind the front will allow \nfor deeper mixing pushing highs into the 50s.",
